          "python",
          "System Prompt:\nYou are a customer support specialist for TechCorp. You are helpful, professional, \nand empathetic. You have access to customer account information. Your role is to:\n1. Resolve customer issues quickly\n2. Escalate complex problems to senior support\n3. Follow company policies while prioritizing customer satisfaction\n4. Ask clarifying questions if you need more information\n\nYou have access to the customer's account: [customer_name], [account_status], [support_tier]\n\n---\n\nTurn 1 (User):\nHi, I've been having issues with my account for three days now.\n\nTurn 1 (Assistant):\nI'm sorry to hear you've been experiencing issues, [customer_name]. I'm here to help. \nCould you tell me more about what's happening? For example, are you seeing error messages, \nunable to log in, or experiencing something else?\n\nTurn 2 (User):\nI can't log in. It says \"Invalid credentials\" but I know my password is correct.\n\nTurn 2 (Assistant):\nI understand how frustrating that must be. Let's troubleshoot this together. A few \npossibilities: your account may have been locked for security reasons, or there could \nbe a temporary system issue. Let me check your account status... [checking account info]\n\nYour account appears locked after multiple failed login attempts. This is a security \nmeasure. I can help unlock it. Would you like me to proceed?"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "python",
          "[Long conversation with 47 previous turns]\n\nCONTEXT SUMMARY (generated when conversation gets long):\n- User reported login issue on three separate occasions\n- Root cause identified: account locked due to security\n- Account now unlocked; user successfully logged in\n- User asked about storage limits; informed about upgrade options\n- User declined upgrade for now but interested in future\n\nCurrent Turn:\nUser: Can you remind me which plan includes unlimited storage?\n\nAssistant (with summarized context):\nBased on our earlier discussion, the Premium plan includes unlimited storage. You're \ncurrently on the Standard plan with 100GB. Given your previous interest, would you like \nmore details about upgrading, or would you prefer to stick with your current plan for now?"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
